largely because earnings per share fell by more

155
00:06:55,154 --> 00:06:57,550
than half in a year and pulled the average down.

156
00:06:58,350 --> 00:06:59,742
Finally, part three.

157
00:06:59,742 --> 00:07:01,968
Starbucks reports after the U.S.

158
00:07:01,968 --> 00:07:03,360
close on October 29.

159
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:07,183
The company expects 2.55 to 2.65 dollars of

160
00:07:07,183 --> 00:07:09,221
earnings per share this year,

161
00:07:09,221 --> 00:07:10,979
excluding one-time costs,

162
00:07:10,979 --> 00:07:13,580
more than 20% above last year's 2.13.

163
00:07:13,770 --> 00:07:16,764
This report will show whether it can keep that outlook.

164
00:07:16,764 --> 00:07:18,560
There are three numbers to check.

165
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:21,620
First, U.S. comparable store sales.

166
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:24,720
The company guided to 6.5% or more this quarter.

167
00:07:24,930 --> 00:07:25,267
Second,

168
00:07:25,267 --> 00:07:27,775
transactions: whether the number of customer visits,

169
00:07:27,775 --> 00:07:28,980
not prices, keeps rising.

170
00:07:29,180 --> 00:07:29,659
Third,

171
00:07:29,659 --> 00:07:34,847
how many dollars Starbucks keeps from every 100 dollars of sales.

172
00:07:34,847 --> 00:07:37,800
It expects more than 11 for the year.

173
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:41,911
In 2008 Schultz closed the stores to retrain on espresso.

174
00:07:41,911 --> 00:07:43,828
In 2024 Niccol brought back mugs,

175
00:07:43,828 --> 00:07:46,210
handwritten notes and a four-minute goal.

176
00:07:46,410 --> 00:07:49,652
Both fixed the in-store experience first.

177
00:07:49,652 --> 00:07:52,499
Whether customer visits keep rising,

178
00:07:52,499 --> 00:07:54,160
October 29 will tell.

179
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:57,363
And one tip for your own money: load only what

180
